{"id": "EUVD-2026-97707", "enisaUuid": "63dfee7b-e371-3e51-8082-26a4542eaeaa", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 contains a memory leak in the YUV encoder, which fails to release allocated memory when a specific operation fails. Attackers can supply crafted input that triggers the failing encoder operation, leaking memory and potentially exhausting resources to cause a denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:32:38", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-69jx-j2x2-g5w4", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/493fab0b6072787e929184761b6ab6405a9486a2", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/3e2075fe4a148ce33e7d749a99898e55a6cad7b5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-memory-leak-in-yuv-encoder"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109263", "GHSA-fhv3-69qw-xpc9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2011ed2f-8d8f-3014-a45f-4532c5c6d033", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}, {"id": "cb6d214b-117b-3250-a3d0-e08427351ebd", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "189995fa-be00-3863-a561-6aef760deaf9", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}